the text first, apply one change by path and write, so two windows on one review keep both their clicks; a failed write changes nothing in memory; `since_review` for a marked file: `""` for a deleted right side, the kept text, else `NoText`, against `Range::right_text`; an unmarked file answers `NoText`). The folder is outside `range/`, so `yamt_range::pair_folders` never lists it. Depends on `yamt-range`, `yamt-gitio` (`Oid`) and `yamt-merge-core` (`compare`) only among `yamt-*`, never on tauri (`scripts/arch-check.sh`). Tests: `tests/reviewed.rs` (marks across new commits, a moved left side, a rename, a deletion, two stores on one review, since-review texts) and `tests/stored_file/` (key text, the pinned folder name and file, refusals, a failed write, a leftover temp file, not a pair folder) over `yamt-conflict-repo` temp repositories.
